enchilada: ADSP stages 4/5: AFE QUAT MI2S RX port start, MAX98927 on SE4, amp tone generator

plan.md Steps 4-5 / §2 (cheapest audible milestone, no PCM path). boot59 verified adsp=3 (q6core answered, AVS 2.8, AFE svc 4 api 2). New boot-arg values; adsp<=3 is unchanged (host check output identical).

adsp=4: stage 3 ends after a 2 s settle instead of the 30 s watch and the ADSP stays up. TLMM gpio58-61 (NORTH) to qua_mi2s (function 1, pinctrl-sdm845.c; 8 mA, no bias, 58/59 output-high as sdm845.dtsi quat_mi2s_*_active). APR to the AFE (svc 4) as q6afe.c does: AFE_SVC_CMD_SET_PARAM / AFE_MODULE_CLOCK_SET / AFE_PARAM_ID_CLOCK_SET for Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_QUAD_MI2S_IBIT 0x106 at 1.536 MHz (sdm845.c MI2S_BCLK_RATE, attribute COUPLE_NO, root default: the clock path mainline sdm845 uses); AFE_PORT_CMD_SET_PARAM_V2 AFE_PARAM_ID_I2S_CONFIG on 0x1006 (16 bit, AFE_PORT_I2S_SD1 per qcom,sd-lines <1>, stereo, 48 kHz, ws internal, 36 bytes = sizeof(union afe_port_config)); AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START; 2 s; then always DEVICE_STOP, clock off, the pins' old cfg back, ad_stop(). Every APR basic result is logged; any failure stops the same way.

adsp=5: with the port running, the MAX98927 (0x3a on QUP SE4 i2c@890000) through a new sweet_amp_reg() in sweet_touch.c that reuses the gauge's GENI FIFO engine (third touch_state; gpio89/90 SOUTH qup4 = mux 2/3; GCC wrap0 AHB 6/7, core 8/9, SE4 14, CBCR 0x174f0, RCG 0x174f4). Reset gpio69 (EAST) low 10 ms then high, REV_ID 0x1ff must be 0x40, then Linux max98927_probe + set_fmt (I2S slave NB_NF) + hw_params (16 bit, 48 kHz, BSEL 32) with the lowest gain: digital volume 0 = -16 dB, speaker gain 0x11 = +3 dB (lowest step that is not mute). The amp is not enabled. adsp=5N (N 1..15, e.g. adsp=51) also writes TONE_GEN_DC_CFG 0x38 = N, SPK_SRC_SEL = tone, AMP_EN, GLOBAL_EN for 1 s: neither Linux nor the OnePlus vendor driver documents the TONE_CONFIG encodings, so N is chosen at boot. Teardown always: GLOBAL_EN/AMP_EN/tone off, soft reset, gpio69 held low (amp in reset).

